          "total_marks": 6,
          "stem_markdown": "The time taken in minutes for a certain daily train journey has a normal distribution with standard deviation 5.8 . For a random sample of 20 days the journey times were noted and the mean journey time was found to be 81.5 minutes.\n\n(a) Calculate a 98% confidence interval for the population mean journey time. [3]\n\n(b) Explain briefly whether this statement is true or not. [1]\n\nTwo independent 98% confidence intervals are found.\n\n(c) Given that at least one of these intervals contains the population mean, find the probability that both intervals contain the population mean. [2]",
          "question_number": 3,
          "mark_scheme_items": [
            {
              "mark_code": "M1",
              "part_path": [
                "a"
              ],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 1,
              "content_markdown": "$81.5 \\pm z \\times \\frac{5.8}{\\sqrt{20}}$",
              "guidance_markdown": "For a correct expression (accept if only one side of the interval calculated). Any z (must be a z).",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                7
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "B1",
              "part_path": [
                "a"
              ],
              "is_final_answer": false,
              "sequence_number": 2,
              "content_markdown": "$z = 2.326$",
              "guidance_markdown": "",
              "source_page_numbers": [
                7
              ],
              "is_alternative_method": false
            },
            {
              "mark_code": "A1",
              "part_path": [
                "a"
              ],
              "is_final_answer": true,
              "sequence_number": 3,
              "content_markdown": "$78.5 to 84.5$ (3sf)",
              "guidance_markdown": "Must be an interval.",
              "source_page_numbers": [
